A leisure-park ride consists of a carriage that moves along a railed track. Part of the track lies in a vertical plane and follows an arc XY of a circle of radius $13\text{ m}$, as shown in Fig. 2.1.
{{figure:figure_2_1}}
The mass of the carriage is $580\text{ kg}$. At point X, the carriage has velocity $22\text{ m s}^{-1}$ in a horizontal direction. The velocity of the carriage then decreases to $12\text{ m s}^{-1}$ in a vertical direction at point Y.

